<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Iazyges</h1><p class="st-meta">20 CE – 375 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Sarmatian horse nomads who settled the plain between the Danube and Tisza and fought Marcus Aurelius before becoming Roman auxiliaries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Iazyges were a Sarmatian people of the steppe north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. In the first half of the 1st century CE they moved west into the plain between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>, wedging themselves between Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dacia">Kingdom of Dacia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were mounted pastoralists led by kings and nobles, famed for armoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">lancers</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> alternately paid and fought them, using them against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacians">Dacians</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcomannic-wars">Marcomannic Wars</a> they invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>; after defeat on the frozen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanticus">Zanticus</a> made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> in 175 CE and sent 8,000 cavalry, many of them posted to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They remained a troublesome neighbour, fighting Constantine and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> in the 4th century. The arrival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> around 375 overwhelmed them, and they were absorbed into the Hunnic sphere and later peoples of the Carpathian basin.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 20 CE – 375 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:60.10%;width:7.06%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>20 CE – 375 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Banadaspus, Zanticus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sarmatian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sarmatian (Iranian)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jazyges, Sarmatian Iazyges</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=198&amp;focus=iazyges" aria-label="Iazyges on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5139 543 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Iazyges lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5459 799L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5459 799h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5459 799h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=198&amp;focus=iazyges">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

